IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cpp-core-age`
IMPORT `cp5-months`
IMPORT `cp5-d-reinstatement`

-- Tests of section 70.1 (cp5-d-reinstatement.l4). Expected values were worked out by hand from the text.

§ `Tests of section 70.1`

§§ `Subsection 70.1(1) and paragraph 70.1(3)(b): within two years`

-- Ceased to receive the pension in March 2020 because they returned to work.
-- Incapable again in March 2022: 24 months after, "within two years".
#ASSERT `s 70.1(1) — the person is entitled to have the disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit reinstated` TRUE (YMD 2020 3 10) (YMD 2022 3 31)
-- April 2022: 25 months, too late.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 70.1(1) — the person is entitled to have the disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit reinstated` TRUE (YMD 2020 3 10) (YMD 2022 4 1))
-- The same month as the ceasing: 0 months, in time.
#ASSERT `s 70.1(1) — the person is entitled to have the disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit reinstated` TRUE (YMD 2020 3 10) (YMD 2020 3 20)
-- Incapable in a month before the ceasing (February 2020): not "again".
#ASSERT NOT (`s 70.1(1) — the person is entitled to have the disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit reinstated` TRUE (YMD 2020 3 10) (YMD 2020 2 20))
-- Did not cease because of returning to work.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 70.1(1) — the person is entitled to have the disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit reinstated` FALSE (YMD 2020 3 10) (YMD 2021 3 20))
-- A count across a year end: December 2020 to February 2021 is 2 months.
#ASSERT `cp5 helper -- the number of months from the month the person ceased to receive it to the month they became incapable again` (YMD 2020 12 31) (YMD 2021 2 1) EQUALS 2

§§ `Subsection 70.1(2): the request, with regulation 71`

-- Became incapable again in March 2022: the request may be made through 31 March 2023 (12 months after the month).
#ASSERT `s 70.1(2) — the request for reinstatement was made in accordance with the regulations` (YMD 2022 3 15) (YMD 2023 3 31) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 70.1(2) — the request for reinstatement was made in accordance with the regulations` (YMD 2022 3 15) (YMD 2023 4 1) TRUE)
-- Across the year end: incapable in December 2021, the last day is 31 December 2022.
#ASSERT `s 70.1(2) — the request for reinstatement was made in accordance with the regulations` (YMD 2021 12 1) (YMD 2022 12 31) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 70.1(2) — the request for reinstatement was made in accordance with the regulations` (YMD 2021 12 1) (YMD 2023 1 1) TRUE)
-- Not in writing.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 70.1(2) — the request for reinstatement was made in accordance with the regulations` (YMD 2022 3 15) (YMD 2022 4 1) FALSE)

§§ `Subsection 70.1(3): the Minister shall approve`

-- Ceased in March 2021; incapable again June 2022 (15 months); born 15 June 1957 (65 reached July 2022): not yet 65.
#ASSERT `s 70.1(3) — the Minister must approve the request for reinstatement` TRUE (YMD 2021 3 10) (YMD 2022 6 10) (YMD 1957 6 15) TRUE FALSE
-- Incapable on 1 July 2022, the day 65 is reached under section 2(2): paragraph (c) fails.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 70.1(3) — the Minister must approve the request for reinstatement` TRUE (YMD 2021 3 10) (YMD 2022 7 1) (YMD 1957 6 15) TRUE FALSE)
-- Paragraph (a) not satisfied.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 70.1(3) — the Minister must approve the request for reinstatement` FALSE (YMD 2021 3 10) (YMD 2022 6 10) (YMD 1957 6 15) TRUE FALSE)
-- Paragraph (b): 25 months elapsed.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 70.1(3) — the Minister must approve the request for reinstatement` TRUE (YMD 2020 3 10) (YMD 2022 4 10) (YMD 1970 6 15) TRUE FALSE)
-- Paragraph (b), exactly 24 months: allowed.
#ASSERT `s 70.1(3) — the Minister must approve the request for reinstatement` TRUE (YMD 2020 3 10) (YMD 2022 3 10) (YMD 1970 6 15) TRUE FALSE
-- Paragraph (c), second limb: a request for a disability pension by a person receiving a retirement pension fails.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 70.1(3) — the Minister must approve the request for reinstatement` TRUE (YMD 2021 3 10) (YMD 2022 6 10) (YMD 1970 6 15) TRUE TRUE)
-- ... but not a request for a post-retirement disability benefit, which only a retirement pension beneficiary can have.
#ASSERT `s 70.1(3) — the Minister must approve the request for reinstatement` TRUE (YMD 2021 3 10) (YMD 2022 6 10) (YMD 1970 6 15) FALSE TRUE

§§ `Subsections 70.1(4), (5) and (6)`

#ASSERT `s 70.1(4) — the Minister must approve the reinstatement of the disabled contributor's child benefit` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 70.1(4) — the Minister must approve the reinstatement of the disabled contributor's child benefit` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 70.1(4) — the Minister must approve the reinstatement of the disabled contributor's child benefit` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 70.1(5) — the Minister must inform the person in writing of the decision whether or not to approve the request` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 70.1(5) — the Minister must inform the person in writing of the decision whether or not to approve the request` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 70.1(6) — the Minister must inform the person in writing of the decision whether or not to approve a disabled contributor's child benefit` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 70.1(6) — the Minister must inform the person in writing of the decision whether or not to approve a disabled contributor's child benefit` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 70.1(6) — the Minister must inform the person in writing of the decision whether or not to approve a disabled contributor's child benefit` FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 70.1(6) — the Minister must inform the person in writing of the decision whether or not to approve a disabled contributor's child benefit` FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§§ `Subsections 70.1(7) and (8): the provisions that do not apply`

-- (7): paragraphs 42(2)(b), 44(1)(b) and (h), 44(2)(a), subsection 44(4), sections 69 and 70.01 do not apply.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 70.1(7) — a provision of the Act applies to a reinstated disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit` `the provision paragraph 42(2)(b)`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 70.1(7) — a provision of the Act applies to a reinstated disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit` `the provision paragraph 44(1)(b)`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 70.1(7) — a provision of the Act applies to a reinstated disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit` `the provision paragraph 44(1)(h)`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 70.1(7) — a provision of the Act applies to a reinstated disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit` `the provision paragraph 44(2)(a)`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 70.1(7) — a provision of the Act applies to a reinstated disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit` `the provision subsection 44(4)`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 70.1(7) — a provision of the Act applies to a reinstated disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit` `the provision section 69`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 70.1(7) — a provision of the Act applies to a reinstated disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit` `the provision section 70.01`)
-- Others apply, including those that (8) excepts for the child's benefit alone.
#ASSERT `s 70.1(7) — a provision of the Act applies to a reinstated disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit` `another provision of the Act`
#ASSERT `s 70.1(7) — a provision of the Act applies to a reinstated disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit` `the provision paragraph 44(1)(e)`
#ASSERT `s 70.1(7) — a provision of the Act applies to a reinstated disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit` `the provision subsection 74(2)`
-- (8): paragraphs 44(1)(e) and 44(2)(a) and subsections 44(4) and 74(2) do not apply.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 70.1(8) — a provision of the Act applies to a reinstated disabled contributor's child benefit` `the provision paragraph 44(1)(e)`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 70.1(8) — a provision of the Act applies to a reinstated disabled contributor's child benefit` `the provision paragraph 44(2)(a)`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 70.1(8) — a provision of the Act applies to a reinstated disabled contributor's child benefit` `the provision subsection 44(4)`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 70.1(8) — a provision of the Act applies to a reinstated disabled contributor's child benefit` `the provision subsection 74(2)`)
#ASSERT `s 70.1(8) — a provision of the Act applies to a reinstated disabled contributor's child benefit` `another provision of the Act`
-- Paragraph 44(1)(h) and section 69 are excepted in (7) only.
#ASSERT `s 70.1(8) — a provision of the Act applies to a reinstated disabled contributor's child benefit` `the provision paragraph 44(1)(h)`
#ASSERT `s 70.1(8) — a provision of the Act applies to a reinstated disabled contributor's child benefit` `the provision section 69`

§§ `Subsection 70.1(9): the least amount`

-- Calculated 800, floor 900, no division: 900.
#ASSERT `s 70.1(9) — the monthly amount of the reinstated disability pension, or of the survivor's pension payable to the person` 800 900 FALSE EQUALS 900
-- Calculated 1000, floor 900: 1000.
#ASSERT `s 70.1(9) — the monthly amount of the reinstated disability pension, or of the survivor's pension payable to the person` 1000 900 FALSE EQUALS 1000
-- Equal: the same amount.
#ASSERT `s 70.1(9) — the monthly amount of the reinstated disability pension, or of the survivor's pension payable to the person` 900 900 FALSE EQUALS 900
-- Subject to a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings: the floor does not hold the amount up (fork F11).
#ASSERT `s 70.1(9) — the monthly amount of the reinstated disability pension, or of the survivor's pension payable to the person` 800 900 TRUE EQUALS 800

§§ `Subsection 70.1(10): when payment begins`

-- Became incapable again on 12 December 2021: payable from January 2022.
#ASSERT `s 70.1(10) — the month with which a reinstated pension or benefit is payable` (YMD 2021 12 12) EQUALS YMD 2022 1 1
#ASSERT `s 70.1(10) — the month with which a reinstated pension or benefit is payable` (YMD 2022 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2022 4 1
